WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.133
-Martha,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.367
-Thank you.
-It's always great

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.534
to have you on.
Thanks for playing "Charades"

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.868
with me and being my partner.
I appreciate it.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.300
-It was so much fun.
-I want to talk about --

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.567
There's so many things.
By the way, I never know

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.834
if I thanked you for this,
but do you remember

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.267
when I ran into you at a farm?

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.801
-Out in the Hamptons?
-Yeah.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.701
-Yeah.
-And you taught me

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.067
how to pickle,
and you got me into pickling.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.467
And I made pickles.
I was --

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.667
-I was so happy
that you wanted to pickle.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.934
[ Laughter ]
-Is that right?

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.434
-So happy.
-I was at this farm --

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:31.067
Fairview Farms.
Harry is the owner there,

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.334
the farmer there.
I love him.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.934
-They're the ones who deep-fry
the sweet potatoes

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.100
and all the -- and the red
potatoes and the blue potatoes.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.167
-It's so delicious.
I just love the whole family,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.801
the vibe, and I'm there,
and I go,

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.000
"Harry, how do you make -- do
you have any pickle recipes?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.968
Or how do you --"
He goes, "I don't really know,

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.267
but she would be
the perfect person to ask."

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.834
I turn around,
and Martha Stewart is at the --

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.400
picking vegetables
at the garden.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.734
I go, "This is like a dream.
This is like unbelievable."

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.234
[ Laughter ]
-You're such a good student.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:56.300
You know, you just
pick it up right away.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.601
And you have a good memory, too.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.167
Because you remembered
how to make them.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.434
-I did, and I loved them.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.734
-I should have brought you
my newest pickles.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.734
I'll send you a jar.
-Oh, my God.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.000
-Little tiny
red and yellow peppers.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.434
Pequeño peppers.
-That's perfect.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.067
See? Come on.
I want to talk about --

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.968
You have a show this weekend
on HGTV called "Table Wars."

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.834
-Oh, yeah.
-You -- That's a giant thing.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.133
Then you're starting Martha.com.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.634
Different than
MarthaStewart.com.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:19.934
This is Martha.com.
-Yes.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:23.167
Yeah, this is our online store
with all our things,

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.501
things that I design,
things that I curate...

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.868
-It's so impressive.
-...things that we find

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.033
here and there.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:31.133
And it's a really, really
wonderful website.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.133
And so it answers
all your needs.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.734
If you're a homemaker and you
need stuff for your kitchen

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.234
or your bedrooms,
your bathrooms, it's there.

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:40.067
But if you need gifts,
they're there.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.100
-Yeah. You have flannel sheets
on there, I saw.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.133
I really checked it out.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:44.934
You have NFTs
you're selling on there.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.300
-Oh, the best.
The best.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.901
And, you know,
I was so surprised, because,

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:51.133
you know, everybody started
getting into the NFTs,

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.801
nonfungible...
-Tokens, yeah.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.033
-...tokens, you know.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:57.367
And you can pay with the
cryptocurrency or without.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:02.300
One of ours, the naughty nurse
picture of me for Halloween,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.334
sold for a lot.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.968
[ Cheering ]
-I was thinking --

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.701
Because you always have
these new ideas.

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.734
I always thought
maybe I'd pitch you an idea,

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.400
and maybe we could get into
business together.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.367
-Let me hear.
-Okay. Ready for this?

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.534
-This is like "Shark Tank."

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.901
I've always wanted to be
on "Shark Tank."

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.300
-Oh, yeah, me too.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.234
-All right, ready?
This one, here we go.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.400
We can go fast or slow
if you want.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.000
Pre-made cranberry slices,
almost like Kraft cheese,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.467
but it's just cranberry slices.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.534
You throw it on a turkey
sandwich with stuffing,

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:34.133
and it's a post-Thanksgiving...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:35.567
All right, all right.
Hey, don't worry --

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:36.767
Hey, don't worry about it.
I got a lot of -- tons of ideas.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:38.601
-How do you package them?
They're messy.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:41.567
Make your own cranberry sauce
and just put a nice little

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:43.934
spoon of it on each sandwich.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:46.634
-Sandwich?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:47.934
-Well, turkey sandwiches
the day after.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.601
-I know, but now you just said
"sandwich,"

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:50.634
but before, you said,
"sandwhich."

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.200
-"Sandwhich."
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.334
-Are you ready for this, Martha?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.367
"Oh, we're having a sandwhich."

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.801
Martha, how about this?
Ready for this?

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.133
-With stuffing! Don't forget
the stuffing on the sandwich.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:02.834
-I know, the stuffing.
Um, cookie bread.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.734
-Cookie bread.
Like what?

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.734
What do you mean?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.734
Oh, they're in for it.
They're into it.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.667
-I'm enjoying
your reaction because --

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.667
-Cookie bread.
-Yeah, so why does

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.000
cinnamon toast
have the only sweet bread

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.934
that you can get out there?
Why not different flavors

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:19.701
of sweet breads, like,
that taste like sugar cookies

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:23.601
or peppermint cookies
or chocolate chip?

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.601
-Why not just eat the cookies?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.868
-You always want, like,
something different.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.067
Okay.
You don't like that.

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:32.067
All right, last idea.
How about coffee mugs

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.033
where, if you put them
on the holder,

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:37.033
a little air blows through
the bottom of them

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.100
and just keeps it
stirring around.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.200
[ Light laughter ]
-Stirring what?

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.200
-No.
-Someone just yelled, "No."

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.200
[ Laughter ]
Well, if you use

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.767
an alternative milk like
a nut milk or something --

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.067
-But, see, I don't like mugs.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:52.534
I think mugs are sort of
clumsy and ugly.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:55.534
[ Laughter ]
I don't own a mug in my house.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.434
-Really?
-No. I have beautiful cups.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.968
-We give you mugs every time
you're on our show.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:03.067
-I know, but I give them away.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:07.200
-Hey, if you guys want our mugs
or anything, go to Martha.com.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Everything holiday.

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:10.467
Check it out.
Recipes.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.267
You'll just love every
single thing on this thing.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.367
Tune in for the premiere
of "Table Wars"

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:17.300
this Sunday night
at 8:00 p.m., on HGTV.

